# Multi-agent local state rules

- Use the initial commit only as the review baseline.
- After work begins, the current local working tree is authoritative.
- Other agents may modify the same files at any time.
- Re-read every target file from the current local working tree immediately before editing it.
- Do not assume a file still matches its state from the beginning of the task.
- Do not discard uncommitted changes that were not created by you.
- Preserve compatible changes made by other agents.
- Integrate with the latest local implementation instead of restoring an older version.
- Resolve logical conflicts by merging the current implementations and rerunning tests.
- Use the initial baseline only for comparison and final reporting, never as a restoration source.
<!-- MEW-MULTI-AGENT_END -->
